                {
                  "id": "b39710fc-896b-44ae-9a8b-5c15a1be15ec",
                  "title": "Plaintext Credential Exposure via Database Leak",
                  "status": "Open",
                  "severity": "TBD",
                  "type": "",
                  "description": "If the User Database is compromised (SQL injection, insider threat, misconfigured access), and passwords are stored as plaintext or weak hashes (MD5/SHA1), all user credentials are immediately exposed.\n",
                  "mitigation": "Store passwords using bcrypt or Argon2 with appropriate cost factors. Never store plaintext. Apply principle of least privilege on DB access, the web server should only have SELECT on the credentials table, not full DB access.",
